// src/config/solutionsSciLedger.ts
//
// SOLUTIONS-SCI (owner approval, 6 Nov 2026) — the VERIFICATION LEDGER for the NCERT Class 10
// SCIENCE solutions pages. Read by `scripts/solutions/selectScienceSolutions.ts`: an id marked
// `ref-mismatch` or `hold` is NOT published; `no-verdict` publishes without a typed ✓/✗.
//
// ★ METHOD — the Maths bar (solutions2Ledger.ts), every pass an independent `claude -p` agent with a
//   fresh context, run over EVERY row that passed the deterministic rules (106 for the SCI-1 pilot,
//   209 more for SOLUTIONS-SCI-2's ten chapters, each chapter file confirmed byte-identical to the
//   current ncert.nic.in jesc1NN.pdf, Reprint 2026-27):
//   1. BOOK CHECK — each row against the full text of its chapter in OUR STORED COPY of the NCERT
//      Class 10 Science textbook (Firebase Storage `ncert/<subject>/ch<N>.pdf`, footer "Reprint
//      2026-27"; text extracted with pymupdf): MATCH / MISMATCH / NOT_FOUND at the cited reference,
//      whether the row's text is FAITHFUL to the 2026-27 book (same data), and whether the book's
//      question depends on a figure or table the row does not carry. Not MATCH → `ref-mismatch`;
//      not faithful or figure-dependent → `hold`.
//   2. SYLLABUS — already screened by code (syllabusGuard.ts Science lists + syllabus2026-27.ts);
//      the auditors also hold any step that teaches content beyond the 2026-27 Class 10 syllabus.
//   3. BLIND SOLVE — EVERY row (not a 20% sample) solved from the question and options ONLY.
//   4. JUDGE + TEXT/STEPS AUDIT — a further agent compared each blind answer with the stored key and
//      re-read every step: any disagreement, a key or step judged wrong, a drafting artifact, or a
//      non-CBSE term → `hold`.
//   5. SECOND AUDIT — a fresh examiner agent re-read every row still publishable after 1-4, tasked
//      only with finding errors; anything flagged → `hold`. The lane builder then spot-read a sample
//      of the remaining rows (MCQs, numericals, a 5-mark row) by hand.
//   6. THIRD AUDIT (review of #1602, 6 Nov) — a fresh agent with the NCERT chapter text and the
//      reviewer's checklist: every requested equation shown and balanced; no merged stems; no
//      figure-less drawing; no mark-bearing step without content; nothing beyond the chapter; no
//      [N mark] on MCQs; no error. Its flags were applied by ONE written rule: HOLD a conceptual
//      restatement / summary / meta / repeated step, a scope term ABSENT from the chapter text (body
//      or figure labels), a key/steps disagreement or an error; KEEP a final-answer step (value +
//      unit, or the conclusion asked for: CBSE marks it), a term the NCERT Class 10 Science
//      textbook itself uses in any chapter, body or figure labels (thermite is NCERT Ch 3; Fig 5.10
//      labels the aorta and venae cavae; SCI-2 grepped every flagged term across all 13 official
//      chapter texts), a drawing answered by its bound solution figure, and [N mark] on MCQs
//      (the Science page strips it on objective rows). The scope test is mechanical: a term the
//      2026-27 textbook never uses (grep of the 13 official chapter texts) holds the row, whoever
//      found it (the audit, or the #1605 review: stoichiometry, moles, photochemical,
//      bidirectional, sinks, warm-blooded). Since the second #1605 review it is a SELECTION RULE
//      (`off-book-term`, scripts/solutions/ncertScienceVocabulary.json), not a manual pass. ONE rule
//      for a summary final step: a final step that states the final value(s) with unit is content; a
//      step that only restates an earlier line with no final value holds the row. Rows are HELD, never edited: the bank is
//      outside this lane.
// ★ CONTENT-BOUND. Each publish entry carries `hash` = rowHash() (selectSolutions.ts) of the question,
//   options, keys, steps and ncertRef the verifiers saw; a changed bank row drops off the page as
//   `unverified` until it is verified again. A candidate not listed here is never published.
// ★ HOLDS are bank-repair work: each note says exactly what is wrong, so a bank lane can fix the row
//   and a later lane can re-verify it (new hash) and publish it.

// ★ SOLUTIONS-SCI-3 (owner instruction 6 Nov 19:49 IST) — NCERT EXEMPLAR Science rows, same ledger.
//   Book check against the OFFICIAL ncert.nic.in Exemplar Class X Science files (jeep101–104,
//   106–113): the owner's staged copies (handoff_6 Nov/exemplar-science) differ from the official
//   files (a 2018 print with a date stamp and a different heading font), so per the owner's 20:07
//   instruction the official text was used. Stages: book check, blind solve of every row, judge,
//   and the #1602-review checklist audit with the 2026-27 NCERT TEXTBOOK chapter as the scope
//   (so Evolution and other deleted content in the old Exemplar chapters is held); the same written
//   rule as step 6 decides its flags. A publish row whose judge overrode a disagreeing blind solve
//   is held.

