  "CTRL-EXMPLR-6-SA-011": { status: "hold", note: "checklist audit: The answer uses glucagon and 'mixed gland', and says the pancreas secretes digestive enzymes. None of this is in the textbook chapter. It also names the pituitary and adrenal positions in ways the chapter does not state. [off-book terms: glucagon, mixed gland]" },
  "CTRL-EXMPLR-6-LA-002": { status: "hold", note: "checklist audit: The answer and steps use cerebrum, pons and medulla oblongata. They also give mid-brain functions (visual and auditory reflexes, eye movements) that are not in the textbook. The textbook gives only fore-brain, mid-brain, hind-brain, cerebellum and medulla. [off-book terms: cerebrum, medulla oblongata, memory, eye movements]" },
  "CTRL-EXMPLR-6-LA-003": { status: "hold", note: "checklist audit: The answer uses meninges, CSF, cranium and the nerve-pair counts, none of which are in the textbook. The textbook says only a bony box with a fluid-filled balloon, and the vertebral column. [off-book terms: meninges, cerebrospinal fluid, cranium, 12 pairs, 31 pairs]" },
  "CTRL-EXMPLR-6-LA-004": { status: "hold", note: "checklist audit: The last step 'Each hormone has specific target tissues' is a filler remark. 'Secondary sexual characters' is not in the textbook. [off-book terms: secondary sexual characters]" },
