  "CTRL-EXMPLR-6-LA-006": { status: "hold", note: "checklist audit: The answer and steps use interneuron and effector, which are not in the textbook. Knee jerk and sneezing are also not in the chapter. The textbook describes the arc as input nerve to output nerve in the spinal cord. [off-book terms: interneuron, effector, knee jerk, sneezing]" },
  "CTRL-EXMPLR-6-LA-007": { status: "hold", note: "checklist audit: The last step 'Hence both are needed...' only restates the conclusion. The step 'Without nerves... without hormones...' repeats earlier steps." },
  "CTRL-EXMPLR-6-LA-008": { status: "hold", note: "checklist audit: The steps use 'negative feedback' and 'glucose uptake', which are not in the textbook. Binding to receptors in target organs is also not described in the chapter. [off-book terms: negative feedback, target organ receptors, glucose uptake]" },
  "CTRL-EXMPLR-6-LA-009": { status: "hold", note: "judge/audit: Key point (3), 'enzymes that release and break down neurotransmitters are arranged only one way', is vague and inaccurate, since enzymes do not release neurotransmitters. Remove it and keep vesicles-only-at-axon-end plus receptors-only-on-dendrite." },
